{
  "description": "The one place `local` does NOT create a new binding. At the root scope there is no enclosing scope to shadow into, so when a `global` of that name already exists `local` leaves it global and `local name = value` assigns the initializer to it (spec/execution-model.md:520-526, spec/commands.md:121) — a second, procedure-invisible binding beside it would hide shared state from every procedure without saying so. `peek` therefore still reads the shared binding and prints `5`, as does the top level. The procedure read is the whole point: measured, an implementation whose root-scope `local` forks the binding away from the global stops at `peek` with `ol-undefined-var` and never reaches the top-level `print` at all, so a fixture that only printed at the top level would report `5` either way.",
